    "granted_by": "Maintainer review, 2026-08-29, across two messages.\n\nApproval: \"The behavioural continuation is approved for paid launch after one final prereg/state-only normalization.\" Reviewer verdict, verbatim: \"continuation science: GO\"; \"implementation/readiness: GO\"; \"existing cumulative cap $283.76: sufficient\"; \"continuation hard ceiling: $8.0691\"; \"no new budget increase is required\"; \"paid launch: GO after the normalization below and exact-launch gates\".\n\nAfter the assistant reported a launch blocker (the continuation computed its executable digest with sha256_json while the shared session_commit_gate independently re-derives SHA256 over sorted path:sha256 lines), the maintainer granted the repair: \"GO for the one-line digest-contract repair. This is a narrow executable-identity fix, not a reopening of continuation science, pricing, or the behavioural-selection design.\" The maintainer further directed: \"the continuation producer must adapt to the established shared contract. Do not modify session_commit_gate and do not add an authorization-specific workaround.\"\n\nLaunch condition, verbatim: \"If every gate passes, launch the behavioural continuation directly without returning for another routine review. If another genuinely new material blocker appears, stop and report.\"\n\nCovers: ONE behavioural-continuation session: import the completed Phase-B Stage-1 and rung-1 state, buy only the genuinely missing behavioural probes (one sb for fe9683e6a9c7, and at worst two conditional sc for fe9683e6a9c7 and the canonical control), apply the frozen pooled sa+sb rule and the frozen final-selection rule, emit the terminal report, retain evidence, tear the pod down and stop.\n\nCumulative spend at approval $260.0550 against a cumulative cap of $283.76.\n\nDoes NOT authorize: Re-buying Phase-B Stage 1 or any search \u2014 Stage 1 is complete, retained and authoritative, and runs_search is False by type. Also excluded: a second attempt; any use of the historical $35.6660 full-Phase-B ceiling; a fourth seed; backfilling rank 6 or 7; probing any of the three searched non-survivors (ab7632b00788, bf5ae3b6ae00, cca699c93f34), which are evidence only; recomputing rung 1; any cumulative-cap increase; post-Phase-B generalization; DEPTH incumbent selection; ATTENTION/FFN/RESIDUAL_WIDTH research; the canonical Stage-1 NLL; formal Stage 2/Stage 3 recovery training; and any new paid session of any kind. The maintainer's words: \"No changes to science, candidate selection, probes, generalization, operator R&D, canonical Stage-1 NLL, or formal Stage 2/3 in this repair.\"\n\nGrant document: logs/autoinit_continuation_b_grant.json",
